  "caption": "Quinn's first day at the gym came with conflicting advice: machines are useless, free weights are scary. So Quinn tried both. At once.\n\nMachines and free weights can both build strength when effort and volume are matched. The right choice depends on the person, their goals and their stage of rehab.\n\nWhat often helps: machines for starting out or targeting one area, adding free weights and real-life moves as capacity grows, and progressing whichever option you'll genuinely train hard with. Rehab often moves from machines toward more functional movement. Machine-only training isn't wasted effort.\n\nIf pain lingers or gets worse during your program, get it assessed rather than just swapping equipment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
